  },
  "reason": "Initial rules show CWE-74 (Injection) and CWE-22 (Path Traversal) as top matches, but the specific mechanism of loading a module from a template path needs more focused retrieval to confirm the weakness mechanism."
}

{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "bm25_search",
  "arguments": {
    "retrieval_query": {
      "source": "template parameter",
      "sensitive_operation": "load_module()",
      "control": "no validation of module path",
      "weakness_mechanism": "code execution from file path",
      "impact": "arbitrary code execution"
    },
    "top_k": 10
  },
  "reason": "The mechanism involves loading a Python module via 'load_module(template)' where 'template' is user-provided. This directly leads to code execution, which aligns with CWE-95 (Eval Injection) and CWE-74 (Injection). The control aspect shows no validation of the module path, supporting these weaknesses."
}

{
  "type": "final",
  "answer": {
    "hypotheses": [
      {
        "cwe_id": "CWE-95",
        "cwe_name": "Improper Neutralization of Directives in Dynamically Evaluated Code ('Eval Injection')",
        "fit_reason": "The 'load_module(template)' operation directly executes code from a file path, which is a classic eval injection vulnerability when the template parameter is user-controlled."
      },
      {
        "cwe_id": "CWE-74",
        "cwe_name": "Improper Neutralization of Special Elements in Output Used by a Downstream Component ('Injection')",
        "fit_reason": "Using user-controlled data (template path) to load a module can lead to remote code execution, which is a form of injection vulnerability."
      },
      {
        "cwe_id": "CWE-22",
        "cwe_name": "Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory ('Path Traversal')",
        "fit_reason": "The template path can be manipulated to traverse directories and load unintended modules, leading to code execution."
      }
    ]
  }
}
